{"candidates":[{"content":"This conjecture contradicts the edge-construction enrichment programme shared by SRC_004, SRC_006, SRC_007, and SRC_011: any enrichment that injects new attack edges before the fixpoint changes the graph on which the grounded extension is computed, so the resulting labels are the skeptical extension of a strict supergraph, not of the admitted graph, and the claim that reinstatement 'remains derived' is vacuously true at best — the derived labeling is a function of injected edges, not of the admitted evidence. REFUTED IF one exhibits an admitted graph G and a polynomial-time enrichment E such that the grounded extension of E(G) restricted to G's vertices equals the grounded extension of G on every node for all admitted G — that is, if any enrichment is label-invariant on every admitted graph, then the contradiction dissolves and the programme is sound.","typicality":0.2,"neighbours":["SRC_004","SRC_006","SRC_007","SRC_011"],"evidence_refs":[{"block":"000000000004","quote":"every attacker of a warrant's validity_node also attacks the warrant's carriage edge"}]},{"content":"This conjecture abstracts the diagnostic overlay programme: every admissible derived diagnostic — suspend_reason (SRC_003), RESIDUE (SRC_009), standing residue (SRC_005), and DefenseWitness (SRC_002) — is a polynomial-time total function of the unique final grounded labeling and the admitted graph, never an input to the fixpoint, so the covering principle is that derived diagnostics are exactly the class of deterministic post-fixpoint annotations and each instance inherits determinism and polynomial cost. REFUTED IF there exists a diagnostic in the neighbourhood whose computation requires reading a pre-fixpoint label, a non-final labeling, or an edge absent from the admitted graph — i.e., if any diagnostic is not a pure function of the final (labels, edges) pair, the abstraction fails.","typicality":0.85,"neighbours":["SRC_002","SRC_003","SRC_005","SRC_009","SRC_011"],"evi